This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

THE GATE SHIPS, AND THAT IS NOT THE SUBJECT THIS FIXTURE NEEDS. self-update-gate.sh lands at
.claude/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/ on every consumer. What a consumer lacks is the
distribution's GIT HISTORY: range.sh finds the newest commit that added a `<!-- CHECK_LOADED:`
anchor with `git log -S` and bounds the range four releases past it, git.decl's `range @range.sh`
line packs that range into the sandbox, and seed.sh installs two consumer trees from its ends. A
consumer repository holds its own history, not core's, so there is no such commit to find and no
range to derive. This is the "corpus only this repo holds" shape.

On a consumer the fixture resolves no core/skills/ path and no distribution .git, prints a
SKIP and exits 0, so the consumer's pool recorded it `ok` on every push while it tested
nothing. The shipped gate's consumer-side behaviour is covered by self-update-gate, which ships.
